---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import FocusedReviews from '../components/FocusedReviews.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
import { pg14Facts } from '../data/facts';
---
<BaseLayout title="PostgreSQL Performance Investigations & Upgrade Reviews | WalStack"
  description="Independent PostgreSQL performance investigations for SaaS teams on RDS, Aurora and self-managed databases. Scope a workload investigation, query review or migration review.">
  <div class="container hero hero-grid">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">Independent PostgreSQL consulting</span>
      <h1>Find what’s slowing down production PostgreSQL.</h1>
      <p class="lede">For SaaS teams facing latency after a release, blocking or rising database load on RDS, Aurora or self-managed PostgreSQL. I trace the symptom to workload evidence and give your team a ranked change plan.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button primary" data-track="primary_cta_click" href="/contact?offer=investigation&amp;from=/">Request an Investigation</a>
        <a class="button ghost" data-track="sample_report_click" href="/sample-report">See Sample Report</a>
      </div>
      <p class="small muted">Work directly with <a href="/about">Kiran Sabne</a>. Fixed quote after fit review.</p>
    </div>
    <aside class="hero-proof"><h2>What changed in production?</h2>
      <ul class="signal-list">
        <li><a href="/problems/postgresql-plan-regression">A query plan changed after a release</a></li>
        <li><a href="/query-rescue">One expensive statement dominates latency</a></li>
        <li><a href="/postgresql-concurrency-and-locking-a-comprehensive-guide">Sessions block or deadlock under load</a></li>
        <li><a href="/database-code-review">A schema migration could interrupt writes</a></li>
        <li><a href="/postgresql-upgrade-readiness">A major upgrade needs a regression baseline</a></li>
      </ul>
    </aside>
  </div>
  <section><div class="container">
    <div class="section-head"><div><span class="eyebrow">PostgreSQL and SQL Server</span><h2>Start with a focused review</h2></div>
    <p>Choose the smallest paid review that answers the decision in front of your team.</p></div>
    <FocusedReviews />
  </div></section>
  <section><div class="container prose">
    <h2>When the decision spans a workload</h2>
    <p><a href="/postgresql-performance-investigation">PostgreSQL Performance Investigation</a> covers a cluster and its dominant workload. Bring latency, CPU, connection pressure or locks that affect several requests.</p>
    <p><a href="/postgresql-upgrade-readiness">PostgreSQL Upgrade Readiness</a> covers compatibility, workload baselines, potential regressions and go/no-go checks for a version change. Community support for PostgreSQL 14 ended on {pg14Facts.communityEol}. <a href="/postgresql-14-eol">Check the managed-service dates</a>.</p>
    <p><a href="/sql-server-performance">SQL Server Performance Review</a> uses Query Store, waits and blocking evidence when the issue crosses statements or application paths.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section><div class="container grid two">
    <div class="prose"><h2>Inspect the work</h2>
      <p>Trace a <a href="/case-studies/lab-generic-plan-regression">prepared-plan regression</a> or a <a href="/case-studies/lab-lock-queue">DDL lock queue</a> through reproducible labs. The <a data-track="sample_report_click" href="/sample-report">synthetic report</a> shows how I present evidence, uncertainty and a validation decision.</p>
      <p class="small muted">The lab cases use generated data; their measurements are not customer results.</p>
      <p>I built <a href={site.planReaderUrl} data-track="planreader_click">PlanReader</a> for inspecting execution plans and the experimental <a href="https://github.com/kiransabne04/pg_stat_index_queries">pg_stat_index_queries</a> project for connecting PostgreSQL indexes to the queries that use them.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card"><h2>How an engagement works</h2><ol>
      <li>Describe the symptom or planned change.</li><li>I confirm fit and send the scope, fee and delivery window.</li>
      <li>Your team shares approved, redacted evidence.</li><li>You receive written findings and checks to run before and after a change.</li>
    </ol><a class="button" data-track="primary_cta_click" href="/contact?offer=investigation&amp;from=/">Request an Investigation</a></div>
  </div></section>
  <section><div class="container cta-panel"><div><h2>Delivering a database change for a client?</h2><p>Agencies and fractional CTOs can bring me in for one database PR, a workload investigation or an upgrade review. We agree who owns client communication and production changes.</p></div>
    <a class="button" data-track="partner_cta_click" href="/partners">Explore a Technical Partnership</a></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
